<%# A single headline stat chip on the owner-only dashboard. Locals: label, value.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.7) —
    docs/design-system/components/analytics/StatChip.prompt.md: "Only two exist in the
    product; they sit side by side with a 12px gap." The gap belongs to the row in
    `analytics/show`, not here, so this partial owns no margin — same rule `ui/_card`
    states for feed cards.

    The surface is now `ui/_card` rather than a hand-written
    `rounded border border-gray-100 bg-white`. That is a real visual change and an
    intended one: Card.prompt.md's first line is "Never round a feed card", and the
    house surface is white + SQUARE + `shadow`, with `#f3f4f6` reserved for hairlines
    INSIDE a card (`ui/_divider`) rather than around one. So the chip loses its 4px
    rounding and its grey edge and gains the card shadow, which is what every other card
    surface in the product already carries. "Card surface", not "every surface": the
    product's other white surface is `ui/_empty_state`, which renders on THIS page a few
    lines below these chips and carries a bare `bg-white` with NO shadow — matching
    docs/design-system/components/core/EmptyState.jsx, which sets a background, padding, a
    gap, a font size and a colour, and no `boxShadow` at all. So on the dashboard the chips
    and the empty state deliberately do not match. Don't "unify" them.

    `padded: true` emits exactly the `px-4 py-3` this file spelled by hand, and the
    remaining utilities ride in `class:`. Deliberately no padding in `class:` — the two
    locals are same-family utilities and Tailwind resolves those by bundle order rather
    than call order, so passing both is a coin flip (see the note in `ui/_card`).

    Type is unchanged: the value is the rare legitimate `font-bold` (readme.md, VISUAL
    FOUNDATIONS: "bold rare") and the label is a 12px `text-grey` micro-label. Neither
    is drift, so neither moves.
%><%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {padded: true, class: "flex-1 text-center"} do %>
  <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary"><%= value %></div>
  <div class="text-xs text-grey"><%= label %></div>
<% end %>
